      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        Hurghada International Airport (HRG) & Red Sea Passenger Guide
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        Hurghada International Airport (HRG / HEGN) is the primary aviation gateway to Egypt's Red Sea Riviera and world-renowned coastal resorts. Located just 5 km southwest of Downtown Hurghada (El Dahar), HRG operates two active passenger terminals: <a href="/airports/hurghada-airport-terminal-1" class="text-indigo-600 font-bold hover:underline">Terminal 1</a> (the futuristic 3-level terminal with modern jet bridges handling European scheduled and charter flights) and <a href="/airports/hurghada-airport-terminal-2" class="text-indigo-600 font-bold hover:underline">Terminal 2</a> (the renovated terminal serving EgyptAir, Air Cairo domestic connections, and regional charter routes).
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Unlike Sinai, all foreign travelers landing at Hurghada Airport require a standard <strong>Egypt Tourist Visa ($25 USD)</strong>, easily purchased at the official 24/7 bank kiosks (Banque Misr / National Bank of Egypt) right before passport control, or via the official online eVisa portal. Pre-booking your <strong>Hurghada airport limousine</strong> guarantees a seamless departure from the terminal: once you clear customs and baggage reclaim, your professional chauffeur is waiting right outside the arrival sliding doors under the covered greeting canopy with your personalized name sign, ready to transport you directly to your resort in El Gouna, Sahl Hasheesh, Makadi Bay, or Soma Bay.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <a href="/airports/hurghada-international-airport" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-amber-600 hover:text-amber-700 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-2 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 transition">
